    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high 83.29 score. His matchup against Painter is the premier play of the day, as a +16% park factor and +16% SP skill adjustment propel his baseline to elite levels. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.11) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.80) are anchored in favorable spots against Elder and Leahy, respectively. Both benefit from high-order placement and positive platoon dynamics, making them the engines of our daily offensive output. While **Jacob Wilson** faces a tougher matchup against Holton, his park adjustment is significant enough to sustain a 63.71 score, cementing him as a core start.\n\nWe continue to prioritize elite sprint speed for our stolen base floor, leading to the inclusion of **Sam Antonacci** (61.43) at the top of the lineup. His matchup against Martinez, N provides a strong SP skill boost, and he remains a priority over **Luis Robert Jr.**, who was our toughest bench decision of the day. Although **Luis Robert Jr.** carries a 52.06 score, the negative platoon adjustment against a right-handed pitcher and lower relative efficiency ratings left him on the outside looking in. We are also keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** and **Coby Mayo**; despite their solid projections, both are contending with risks associated with Painter\u2019s delivery and variable platoon splits, necessitating careful monitoring as the official lineup reports finalize.\n\nThe primary risk today involves the sub-optimal matchups for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** against Suarez. While **Andy Pages** receives a minor efficiency boost from the opponent's slow delivery\u2014a critical factor for our SB-weighted strategy\u2014both players remain near the lower end of our starting thresholds. Furthermore, **Jackson Merrill** faces Whisenhunt in a matchup where his negative platoon adjustment slightly dampens an otherwise favorable SP xERA environment. We will look for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** to carry the heavy lifting to ensure we remain competitive in HR and RBI while maintaining our aggressive stance on the basepaths.",
